<title>USA: U.S. to donate wheat to Tajikistan - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. to donate wheat to Tajikistan - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department said it would donate 6,000 tonnes of U.S. commodities to Save the Children, a charity, for distribution to needy people in Tajikistan.</p>
<p>Donated commodities would include 4,900 tonnes of wheat flour, 600 tonnes of vegetable oil and 500 tonnes of rice.</p>
<p>About 1,600 would be used in feeding programs and 4,400 tonnes will be used as wages in food for work projects.</p>
</text>
